"comparison": "Both AMD and Intel identify specific technical and performance factors that determine product competitiveness in the data center market. AMD lists 'performance', 'energy efficiency', and 'software and hardware compatibility' as main factors. Intel specifically highlights these same factors in the context of cloud workloads, stating that competitive importance relies on 'product performance; energy efficiency; feature differentiation; product quality... and product security and security features.' However, Intel uniquely emphasizes the role of 'collaboration and customization with cloud service provider customers' as a critical competitive driver, a factor not explicitly cited by AMD in this disclosure.",
